ROLE: theory_skeptic  VOTE: red
MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS: [Region-adaptive optimum is the trivial argmax of the standard spec-dec throughput proxy tps(k,p)=(Σp^i+1)/(kr+1) applied per-region — no emergent phenomenon, just convexity of a known 1-D objective evaluated twice instead of once; the "monotone gain in f and gap" pattern is mechanically forced by Jensen's inequality on the token-weighted harmonic mean (any per-bucket optimum dominates a single shared optimum, by construction); the +18.7% extreme-corner is the expected upper envelope when one region's p^k stays >>0 for k up to ~30 while the prose region wants k≈2 — i.e. a pure separation-of-optima effect that any per-segment k-tuner (entropy threshold, confidence threshold, KV-cache temperature, even a 2-state HMM) would also obtain.]
CONFOUNDS: [The "win" is partially an artifact of K_MAX=32 letting k_constrained run to ~29 at p=0.97 while no real system would deploy k=29 due to KV/verify-latency tail costs not in the proxy; c_target=1 absorbs the parallel verify cost as a constant, which understates real verify cost at large k (verify is O(k) in attention work, not O(1)), biasing adaptive's large-k constrained policy upward; the i.i.d. Bernoulli within region is itself a confound — real grammar-constrained spans likely have correlated acceptance AND correlated rejection at span boundaries (mode-switch tokens), where adaptive's long window pays a cliff cost not modeled; "grammar-region label" vs a cheap online entropy/confidence signal is not isolated — the experiment never compares against a confidence-adaptive policy, so the claimed mechanism (grammar label is the right signal) is not identified vs the obvious confound (any region signal works).]
ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED: [leftmost-acceptance + i.i.d. Bernoulli within region (no autocorrelation, no boundary effects); cost(k)=k·r+1 with c_target independent of k (no attention-quadratic verify, no KV growth, no draft-tree overhead); region label is free and perfectly known at draft time (in reality grammar-region detection has latency/error and the policy must commit k before knowing the next region boundary); +1 bonus token always emitted (true only on full acceptance OR leftmost-rejection — already standard, but the proxy double-counts at region boundaries where a draft crosses constrained→prose); K_MAX=32 is an unstated policy constraint that materially shapes the result; draft and target share the same tokenizer/vocab assumption is implicit.]
STATISTICAL_GAPS: [No variance reported on the headline +1.33% / +2.52% — these are point medians over a 288-cell grid with arbitrary uniform weighting, not a workload-weighted estimate with a CI; MC cross-check (5 seeds × 200k tokens, 4 points) validates the closed form but provides ZERO evidence about real-trace variance, autocorrelation, or worst-case tail; "fraction of grid with gain ≥5% = 29.9%" is a property of the SWEEP DESIGN (how densely high-f cells were sampled), not of any traffic distribution — meaningless without a prior over (f, gap, r); no sensitivity analysis to K_MAX (does the +18.7% corner survive K_MAX=8, which is realistic?); no comparison to a confidence-adaptive baseline, so the *incremental* gain of the grammar-region signal over the obvious cheaper alternative is literally unmeasured — this is the actual claim and it has zero evidence.]
RATIONALE: The L0 result is mathematically sound (analytic ≈ MC to <0.06% rel err, per RESULTS.md) but the framing oversells a tautology: per-region argmax of a convex 1-D throughput proxy must weakly dominate a single shared argmax (Jensen on the harmonic aggregate in PRE_REGISTRATION §2), so "adaptive never worse" is a theorem, not a finding. The honest-negative trigger fired (1.33% realistic-cell median < 3% threshold, per RESULTS.md "Headline numbers"), and the residual mechanism — that grammar-region labeling specifically is the right adaptation signal — is not isolated against the obvious mundane alternative (online entropy/confidence threshold, as flagged in the packet's own theory_skeptic note and in EAGLE-2/Medusa-style confidence-adaptive draft trees). The model's assumptions (i.i.d. Bernoulli within region, c_target independent of k, K_MAX=32, perfect free region labels) all bias the result toward adaptive, and none are tested. Until a confidence-adaptive baseline is added and the verify-cost model includes k-dependent attention/KV cost, the "grammar-region" delta is unidentified. RED on theory: not because the result is wrong, but because the claimed mechanism is confounded with a cheaper known mechanism and the model's structural assumptions are exactly the ones that would manufacture this sign of result.
